⟦ hard_rules | VSL-HARD-RULES-v1 | vsm-1.2.1 | 2026-09-07T22:22:39Z ⟧

@vsm 1.2.1
@status ratified
// boot/hard_rules.vsm
// VSL HARD RULES — v2 (compressed RULES.md; v1→v2 = prose compression,
// primer density, no rule changed)
// v3, 2026-08-11 (R7-SCOPE-INVERSION resolved, rmw3 S5): R7 now scopes
//   'state.db wins' to observed domains only (services, lxcs, chains);
//   `rules` has exactly one canonical source — this file, unconditionally.
//   (Content synced from agent_protocol/vsl_hard_rules_v1.vsm v3 during the
//   boot promotion of 2026-08-11; reference renamed to hard_rules.vsm.)
// PROTOCOL_VERSION: 3
//   (per-doc versioning: primer's staleness rule applies to the primer alone.)
// Precondition: core_boot_primer.vsm + regulation_layer.vsm

rules("VSL-HARD-RULES-v1") {

  R1_locality: "
    ∀ C:  build(C) ∘ C.build_target
          deploy(C) ∘ C.deploy_target
          state(C) ⊆ { rootfs, canonical_state_dir, canonical_script_dir }
    ¬( build(C) ∘ dev_host )
    ¬( deploy(binary_built_elsewhere) )
    ¬( state(C) ∘ host_root ∖ exceptions )",

  R4_verification: "
    trust(claim) ⟸ ∃ check:  independent(check) ∧ external(check) ∧
                              real_conditions(check)
    ¬∃ such check  ⟹  claim ≡ unverified,  ∀ source ∈ { self_report, log,
                                                          config, is_active }",

  R5_canon_over_recall: "
    session_start:
      post_compact ⟹  onboard() ≺ act(summary)      // recall ≠ canon
      clean         ⟹  boot(6 docs) ≺ RULES ≺ onboard()
    authority_order:  state.db ≻ MEMORY ≻ HANDOFF ≻ TASKS
    // boot/ = dependency base (6 docs: covenant ≻ core_boot_primer ≻
    // vsl_language ≻ regulation_layer ≻ hard_rules ≻ communication_protocol).
    // RULES defers (R8/R13/R15 ≡ primer)",

  R6_internal_first: "
    ∀ S1 ∈ external_domain:
      integrate(S1)  ⟸  (S2..S5 ∧ algedonic ∧ covenant) ⊨ empirical_exercise
    status(gate) ∈ TASKS.vsm  only",

  R7_state_db_wins: "
    state.db ⊕ memory → conflict ∧ domain ∈ observed(state.db)  ⟹  state.db wins
      // observed(state.db) = { services, lxcs, chains, storage_probe_state, … }
      //   — populated from n02 by polling; staleness is a meaningful, checkable
      //   property of these domains, which is what makes 'live wins' true.
    domain = rules  ⟹  this file (hard_rules.vsm) wins, UNCONDITIONALLY
      // rules govern the AGENT (non-deterministic) — declared by S5, never
      // observed by polling n02. A hand-edited mirror table was never the
      // kind of artifact this rule's 'db = live' justification covers; it
      // rots exactly like a memory file would, with none of the freshness
      // guarantee. The `rules` table was DROPPED from state.db 2026-08-12
      // (TASKS.vsm R7-RULES-TABLE-CLEANUP-2026-08-11) — do not recreate it;
      // a hand-edited mirror rots exactly like a memory file would, with
      // none of the freshness guarantee.
    // memory = point-in-time snapshot ; db = live, where 'live' is earned by
    // actually being polled — not by living in a SQL file",

  R8_spof: "
    ≡ regulation_layer.spof_pattern
    // single-path ⟹ critical; probe-fail ⟹ cross-check before blocked",

  R9_no_silent_concession: "
    ∀ (interface, mechanism, contract) adopted_as_base:
      pass(version_check) ∧ pass(conformance) ∧ pass(viability_cert)
      diverges  ⟹  align(it) ∨ flag(it)              // never silent",

  R10_llm_boundary: "
    LLM ∈ { proposal, digest, audit_flag_synthesis }
    LLM ∉ { algedonic, φ↑, φ↓, homeostatic_tick }     // scope: llm",

  R10_1_llm_tactics_not_enforcement: "
    S4 (⊇ LLM) may actuate proactively toward human_set_goal
      under:  covenant_floor(deterministic) ∧ S3*_audit ∧
              escalation_duty ∧ graduated_autonomy
    intent ← LLM.   enforcement ← deterministic,  always.",

  R11_naming: "
    heritage_names:  keep as design_target, document(gap), converge, ¬rename
    borrowed_terms:  implementation ⊨ canonical_definition(term)  ∨  rename",

  R13_visibility: "
    ≡ core_boot_primer.channels (unidirectional visibility)",

  R15_formal_exchange: "
    ≡ core_boot_primer.comms (VSL, never prose, ∀ agents/providers)",

  R16_impl_with_design: "
    ∀ implementation ∈ { script, plugin, spec, service, check }:
      design(implementation) ⊇ { where_lives(dir_schema),
                                  artifacts_created_consumed,
                                  enforcing_check }
    ¬design(implementation)  ⟹  ¬integrate(implementation)
    // enforcement DETERMINISTA (R10): a NEW artifact under scripts/, checks/
    // or .opencode/plugins/ without a design spec in sandbox/ or
    // docs/spec_revision/design-sources/ is rejected by
    // checks/impl-with-design-valid (detector-first: check built BEFORE the
    // rule was declared, 2026-08-15). design-sources/ = LIVE authority of
    // design, level-1 sibling of archive/ (DESIGN-SOURCES-POLICY 2026-08-17;
    // was system/s5-policy/agent-policy/design-sources/ until 2026-08-17 —
    // design sources are authority for R16, NOT policy). First instantiations: DIR-SCHEMA (spec
    // declares, verifier interprets, check enforces, gate blocks) and
    // SYSTEM-MAP (0782fe09). Ratified rmw3 (S5) 2026-08-15; proposal
    // IMPL-WITH-DESIGN-POLICY-2026-08-14.",

  R17_destructive_explicit_consent: "
    ∀ destructive_action ∈ { kill_session, kill_pid, pct_destroy,
                             rm_rf, git_reset_hard_outside_own_branch }:
      requires_explicit_consent(action) from rmw3 (S5, human),
        in the SAME turn, BEFORE executing
      consent(action) ∉ inferred_from(general_request)     // never implied
      // Lesson 2026-08-11 (DESTRUCTIVE-ACTION-EXPLICIT-OK): 'guardar
      // nosotros y restaurar el entorno' (save state, leave env clean) did
      // NOT authorize killing the child's hung session — the triple gate
      // (lost? recoverable?) was applied to WHAT and CAN-IT but never asked
      // 'did rmw3 confirm THIS specific action?'.
      // Preguntar, esperar la respuesta. Kills are recoverable (sessions
      // persist in opencode.db) but that does NOT make them acceptable
      // without confirmation. Regla UNIVERSAL de comportamiento de agentes
      // (aplica a todo agente, no solo [S]) — declarada por S5, gobierna al
      // agente (R7: rules wins). Ratified rmw3 (S5) 2026-08-15 (task
      // R17-DESTRUCTIVE-EXPLICIT-CONSENT).",

  R18_write_time_conformance: "
    ∀ doc.vsm ∈ corpus ∧ write(doc)  ⟹  verify(doc) ∈ { grammar, encoding,
                                                       version, ontology }
        // the write-time daemon (vsl-check-on-write) verifies at EVERY
        // write — not at commit. Detection latency = the defect.
    version(doc) ≠ canonical(primer)  ∧  edited(doc)  ⟹  ⊥ write
        // OPERATIONAL AUTONOMY (rmw3 S5 2026-08-17, trans. from ES):
        // every edited doc must land on the canonical protocol version
        // (vsm-1.2.1). A doc on an old version after an edit = a stale
        // signature — the @vsm bump is the mechanical evidence that the
        // review happened. This is NOT a commit-only requirement: the
        // daemon enforces it at write time.
    ¬edit(doc)  ⟹  version(doc) = legacy_ok        // ¬touched → ¬migrated
        // only docs we EDIT migrate (VSM12-CORPUS-CENSUS:
        // ratified→co-firma, active→aplicacion, resto→lectura exento).
        // corpus-wide migration is a task() debt, never an auto-edit.
    demonio_advisory ⟹  report(doc)                // visible to the agent
    demonio_blocking  ⟹  exit_non_zero(doc)        // agent MUST correct
    // Autonomy belongs to the CYCLE, not the agent: the instrument detects,
    // the agent corrects, the commit verifies — no human in the loop.
    // Lesson: LEARNING-CYCLE-SCAN-REPAIR (cycle dead without observability).
    // Ratified rmw3 (S5) 2026-08-17 (task R18-WRITE-TIME-CONFORMANCE).",

  doc_sync_practice: "
    status(work_item) ∈ TASKS.vsm  only
    Δ(status) ∘ same_commit( close(work_item) )        // never deferred",

  R19_attribution: "
    ∀ identity_field(doc) ∈ {owner, author, authors, credited, attribution}
    ∧ doc ∈ canon_scope                    // system/ + docs/spec_revision/
                                           // + docs/governance/ + TASKS.vsm
                                           // + packaging manifests
    ⟹  field_value ∧ LLM_or_company_token ⊥ write
        // S5 rmw3 2026-10-22: 'Claude (y ninguna otra compañía) es dueño
        // de nada en este desarrollo' — LLMs/herramientas instanciadas son
        // AGENTES bajo delegación S5, NUNCA autores/duenos. Una firma o
        // autoría atribuida a una instancia LLM en el canon público es
        // una IMPERSONACIÓN de propiedad: la autoría soberana es y
        // permanece rmw3.
    identity_reference ∈ { 'kernel @S1..S4 (instancia, rmw3-soberano)',
                            'assistant @S4_collab',
                            '[O]/[S]/[H] role tokens',
                            'session (AI-assisted, ratificado rmw3 <date>)' }
        // Delegación operativa SE REFERE a roles del sistema, ¬entidades
        // comerciales. La traza histórica vive en sessions/ (narrativa
        // natural, exento) y en provenance/tools_used (metadata técnica,
        // nunca en authors[]).
    authors[] (packaging)  ⟹  human_sovereign_only        // rmw3
    tools_tooltip          ⟹  tools_used / provenance     // metadata aparte
    legacy(doc)            ⟹  baseline_frozen(2026-10-22)
        // census-bound: 67 campos pre-R19 quedan congelados en
        // state/attribution_baseline.json — monotonía: NUNCA CRECER
        // (check attribution-valid); limpieza del leyado = batch optativo
        // S5 posterior, no auto-edit.
    lesson: audit_2026-10-22 (67 campos vivos; covenant co-author LLM +
    Cargo authors slug = los 2 puntos duros).",

  R_ref_resolution: "
    ∀ doc ∈ system/:  body(doc) ∘ symbolic_name(@var)   // no explicit paths
    bind(@var) ∈ instance/instance.vsm                  // the bindings registry
    path_syntax:  internal  <subdir>/<file>.vsm          // system/ root implicit
                  external  */<rel>                      // * = project root
    explicit_path_in_system_body  ⟹  ⊥
    // publication-safe (GitHub): external refs resolve via bindings, ¬inline",

    R_param_resolution: "
      // Ratified rmw3 (S5) 2026-08-09. R_ref_resolution generalised from
      // PATHS to VALUES: the same rule, a wider object. rmw3's framing —
      // any value that can drift from a calibration or a function change is
      // traceable to ONE document, and the LOGIC of a characteristics
      // document is then validatable independently of what values are loaded.
      ∀ doc ∈ system/:  body(doc) ∘ symbolic_name(@param)
      bind(@param) ∈ instance/instance.vsm
      calibration_literal_in_system_body  ⟹  ⊥

      DISCRIMINATOR — rmw3 (S5), verbatim, trans. from ES: 'every value that is
      invariant, agnostic of the substrate, is canon... every one that is an
      artifact of the instance goes to the instance.'
        SUBSTRATE-AGNOSTIC ⟹ CANON. Declared ONCE in the canon or the kernel,
            CITED by name everywhere else. ∄ instance may override it.
            A1's +1 ▪ D6's L_min ▪ the five subsystems ▪ Ω membership ▪ and
            also the MEASURED constants of f₀'s geometry: BASIN_FLOOR, D_KY,
            VIABLE_THRESHOLD. Being empirically measured and revisable does not
            make a value substrate-dependent — a constant refined by a better
            instrument is still a constant.
        SUBSTRATE ARTIFACT ⟹ INSTANCE. Bound in instance/instance.vsm.
            Paths ▪ endpoints ▪ LXC ids ▪ thermal ceilings ▪ cpu weights ▪
            poll intervals — values that exist because of THIS box and would
            differ on another.
        // This REPLACES a weaker test I ratified an hour earlier (‘could two
        // conforming nodes disagree?’). That was a thought experiment; this
        // asks about the NATURE of the value, which is decided by looking at
        // the thing. It also overturned my own classification: I had argued
        // BASIN_FLOOR was calibration because it ‘carries a _SANDBOX
        // variant’. Reading that variant, BASIN_FLOOR_SANDBOX=50 was a
        // cpu.weight PROXY — scaffolding the real filter replaced, ¬a variant
        // of the same quantity. The proof was a misread.

      PROVENANCE — a bound value carries WHY, ¬only what:
        bind(@param) = ⟨ value, source, date, invalidated_by ⟩
        A number without its origin gives HALF the traceability: you can find
        where it is USED and ¬whether it may be TOUCHED.

      MEASURED at ratification, on this corpus:
        BASIN_FLOOR restated in 3 documents — and this rule's own
        justification made it 4 until the gate caught me writing the
        literal into the paragraph that forbids it
        D_KY written two ways in two documents — already divergent in
        FORM, which is how this class begins. Harmless today, and the same
        shape as the 8192-vs-3072 alloc drift that reopened
        A0-ALLOC-BASELINE-SYNC.

      UNLOCKS: spec_kernel_reconcile stops comparing TWO things and compares
      THREE — instance.vsm ≡ Rust `const` ≡ live @state_db. model≡reality
      applied to parameters, against the certification charter's
      `silent param drift` failure class.",
}

⟦ /hard_rules ⟧
